  "story": {
    "who": "Rebecca Warren is a sculptor. According to the gallery's own website, her work moves between figuration and abstraction, and it both draws on and sends up the work of men such as Willem de Kooning and Alberto Giacometti. The gallery adds that ideas about authorship and authenticity, along with literary, psychological and pop-cultural influences, are filtered and distorted as they take three-dimensional form.",
    "then": "Maureen Paley's own website describes a 2011 show, Come Helga, This Is No Place For Us II, as the third time Warren had a solo exhibition there. It included a hand-painted bronze and a work in reinforced clay.",
    "worth_knowing": [
      "The 2011 show at the gallery included a clay work called National Geographic, set on a painted plinth."
    ],
